+    """The detector's click on a born pair as the split's continuation (the owner's orders of 2026-10-28, 02:59 and 04:01 UTC: the click solution built locally, no cosine in the code): a fitting's two children are one singlet from the birth to the first click of either; each detector turns the twins by its own quaternion (`bell_turn`, from the turns the run hands over, the choice between each end's two made outside the board) and splits them by the split's own draw, the up twin where c (W_up + W_down) < room W_up (bobs.splits), the winds the twins' squared Gaussians; the first child's twins stand equal, so it splits half and half, and its answer closes the partner's twins to the opposite twin turned by the first quaternion; the partner's detector turns them back by its own (its conjugate) and splits them, so Born's odds come from the twins alone. Two clicks of one pair in one strike take the - end first by its role. The answers are readings in the credit lines (no gear written), the rewind cutting them with the log; nothing where the run hands over no detectors. A local build for David's verification."""
